# Cloudflare Pages security headers for the static marketing/join site.
# script-src has NO 'unsafe-inline': each executable inline <script> in site/**/*.html is
# allowed by its SHA-256 hash instead, so injected markup cannot run script (audit F-06).
# Do not edit the hashes by hand. After changing an inline script run
# `node scripts/csp-hashes.mjs --write`; tests/site-csp.spec.ts and `npm run build:site`
# fail if this list and the pages drift apart. (JSON-LD blocks are data, not executed, and
# need no hash.)
# style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' deliberately: the marketing build (Tailwind/React) and the
# static pages use inline style attributes and <style> blocks. Style injection is a much
# weaker primitive than script injection and CSS-only exfiltration is blocked by
# connect-src/img-src/font-src, so the cost of nonce-ing every style outweighs the benefit.
# The remaining directives block framing, object embeds, and cross-origin exfiltration.
#
# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups isolates the browsing context group
# but still lets the app open provider/checkout tabs. Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy:
# same-site stops third parties embedding or hot-linking our assets (images, scripts, wasm).
#
# HSTS is set here as well as by helmet on the API, because this site serves
# the invite/join flow and the tokens that go with it. `preload` is
# deliberately omitted: submitting to the browser preload list is effectively
# irreversible for months and would bind every current and future subdomain to
# HTTPS. Add it only as a separate, deliberate decision once every subdomain is
# confirmed HTTPS-only.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-KQIs7Jr13j3VDIIMUDNRwBUWBbH9Bk01sbyF0CiNZ6w=' 'sha256-Y0RFDgNxaSarV5gGm2RcV00pgUtl+I24C1GlgbWSC0Q='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; media-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-site

# Apple fetches this through its CDN and requires application/json. The file
# is deliberately extensionless (Apple mandates the exact name), so Pages has
# nothing to infer a type from and would otherwise serve it as a generic
# binary stream, which the CDN rejects — Universal Links then silently fall
# back to opening Safari with no error anywhere.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
